1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,600
The Moon is moving away from Earth.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,800
NASA's laser measurements reveal…

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:11,000
About 3.8 centimeters per year.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,200
The reason? Ocean tides.

5
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:17,000
Earth's rotation pulls the tidal bulge ahead.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
That tug transfers energy into the Moon's orbit.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,800
Scientists bounce lasers off reflectors on the Moon.

8
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:30,300
They time the return to measure its distance.

9
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,000
A tiny drift—about as fast as fingernails grow.
